    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW217rvRPAeUUaadDdTZqZRwo)_\n\nThird of three stacked PRs. **Based on #326**, which is based on #325: merge in that order, retargeting each to `main`.\n\n## What\n- New module `sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks-widget` registers a `vulpea-ui` widget, `grouped-backlinks`, at order 310 (right after the standard `backlinks` widget at 300).\n  - Registered like the Link inbox widgets in `sp-tab-inbox`: a `vui-defcomponent` plus `vulpea-ui-register-widget`.\n  - Shows the note `vulpea-ui` shows (`use-vulpea-ui-note`), so it follows the main note with the rest of that sidebar. The sidebar's follow toggle does not apply to it.\n  - Each group is its name and count, then a `vulpea-ui-note-link` per note (opens in the main window).\n  - Reuses `sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks-sorted`, so the Org view, sidebar and widget agree.\n- It is a separate file so `sp-vulpea-grouped-backlinks` needs neither `vulpea-ui` nor `vui` at load time. `sp-vulpea-ext` requires it after the grouping module (`vulpea-ui` is loaded by then through `sp-vulpea-ui`).\n- Literate doc (`sp-vulpea.org`, now twelve files) and the module table in `README.org` updated; the commentary no longer says \"NOT YET a widget\".\n\n## Tested\n- 18 ERT tests pass in Emacs 29.3 (4 new for the widget: registration and order, the groups and the count, \"No backlinks\", nothing without a note).\n- The `vui` macros and `vulpea-ui` functions are **stubbed**: the tests check the shape the component returns, not real rendering. I did not run the real `vui`/`vulpea-ui` code.\n- **Not run** in the real Emacs: widget layout, collapse state (it follows `vulpea-ui-default-widget-collapsed`) and the `:indent` on the nested stack are worth a look in the sidebar. To try: open a note that others link to under a meta key, then `C-x t s`.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edit, per the nightly-tidy rule.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAyV71uz259d2Xv3kV)_",
